    <DataNode elementId="AT4G08870-MONOMER" textLabel="AT4G08870-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT4G08870-MONOMER" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="600" centerY="495" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">Arabidopsis genome has two copies of arginase, ARGAH1 and ARGAH2. Co-transformation of ARGAH1 or ARGAH2 with the Arabidopsis arginine decarboxylase ACD2 was able to complement a yeast putrescine mutant. Further more, agmatinase activity at low substrate concentration was detected in ARGAH2 in an in vitro enzyme assay. Both ARGAH2 and ACD2 were shown to locate in the chloroplast. The two genes were co-expressed under stress conditions such as drought, oxidative stress, wounding, and methyl jasmonate treatments.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT4G08870-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-10019, RXN-12670" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="2" />
      <Property key="GOTerms" value="GO:0009507" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT4G08870.1" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT4G08870" />
      <Property key="^citations" value="28716421:EV-EXP-IDA:3728930071:zhang" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <Property key="Locations" value="CCI-CHLOROPLAST-PL" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_28716421" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT5G60540-MONOMER" textLabel="glutaminase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q8LAD0" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="575" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The protein encoded by the &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; gene &lt;i&gt;PDX2&lt;/i&gt; was shown to have glutaminase activity |CITS:[17468224]|. Mutants defective in this gene are arrested at the globular stage of embryo development.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT5G60540-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT5G60540.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q8LAD0" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="glutaminyl-tRNA synthase (glutamine-hydrolyzing)" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33565, RXN-ARA-430" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="2" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT5G60540.1" />
      <Property key="ComponentOf" value="CPLX-8103" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT5G60540" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_17468224" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT2G39800-MONOMER" textLabel="AT2G39800-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="P54887" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="575" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The mothbean delta1-pyrroline-5-carboxylate synthetase (P5CS) has both gamma-glutamyl kinase and glutamic-gamma-semialdehyde dehydrogenase activities. The two enzymatic domains correspond to the ProB and ProA proteins of |FRAME:TAX-562 &lt;i&gt;Escherichia coli&lt;/i&gt;|. The gamma-glutamyl kinase activity of the mothbean P5CS is 50% inhibited by 6 mM proline. The E.coli gamma-glutamyl kinase (ProB) is 30 times more sensitive to proline feedback regulation, which showed a 50% inhibition at 0.2 mM proline |CITS: [1384052]|. A point mutation that changed the residue 129 of the mothbean P5CS from alanine to phenylalanine significantly reduced the proline feedback inhibition |CITS: [7657626]|. There are two P5CS genes in the Arabidopsis genome. Both genes are induced by drought, salt and ABA. The two genes are however differentially regulated at tissue level. The AtP5CS1 gene is expressed in non-dividing mature tissues, whereas, the AtP5CS2 gene is mainly expressed in dividing tissues |CITS: [9351242]|. There are two P5CS genes in Medicago. Measurement of transcripts level of the two genes under normal and salt-stressed conditions indicated that P5CS1 is the housekeeping isoform and that P5CS2 is a stress-specific isoform |CITS: [15032841]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT2G39800-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT2G39800.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Smr" value="P54887" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Prints" value="PR00474" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pride" value="P54887" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Interpro" value="IPR036393" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pfam" value="PF00171" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Phylomedb" value="P54887" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Prosite" value="PS01223" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="P54887" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="&amp;delta;1-pyrroline-5-carboxylate synthetase" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-24272, RXN-12867" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="2" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT2G39800.1" />
